## Hints

- E1: G = 1.1 × 0.9 × 1.1 = 1.089 — the per-day geometric mean is its cube
  root minus one.
- E3: at daily-rebalanced leverage L, arith mean scales by L but variance by
  L² — the drag grows quadratically; CAGR(L) ≈ L·μ − L²σ²/2 (per period).
- E4: 12 × 1% assumes no variance; honest growth = (1.01)¹² − 1 ≈ 12.68%...
  but with 4% monthly vol the drag is ≈ σ²/2 × 12 ≈ 0.96%/yr — smaller than
  you'd think here; compute it exactly.
